## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a production-grade multi-tenant pipeline with strict data isolation, governance, and cost controls across GCP services, plus a robust testing and rollback strategy.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant data isolation with per-tenant Cloud Storage and per-tenant BigQuery datasets
- Dataflow pipeline correctness, idempotence, and scheduling
- IAM and IAM Conditions for least privilege
- Cross-region DR, data residency, and backup strategy
- Cost visibility with labels and budgets

## Code Example

```javascript
class ValidateAndEnrich {
  process(element) {
    if (!valid_schema(element)) return;
    const enriched = enrich(element);
    return enriched;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle schema changes across tenants without downtime?
- How do you enforce per-tenant security boundaries in a shared data lake?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design a scalable, compliant data ingestion path for many tenants, balancing privacy, residency, and cost. Emphasizes correct use of Dataflow, BigQuery per-tenant, CMEK, DLP, and Private Service Connect, plus robust DR.

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub → Dataflow streaming
- Per-tenant BigQuery datasets and residency
- CMEK and DLP for PII
- IAM least privilege and per-tenant service accounts
- Private Service Connect, VPC, Shared VPC
- Cost optimization: partitioning, data lifecycle
- DR: cross-region replication and failover testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example masking function for streaming records
function maskPII(record) {
  if (!record) return record;
  if (record.email) record.email = record.email.replace(/[^@]+@[^.]+(\..{2,})/g, "***@***.***");
  if (record.phone) record.phone = record.phone.replace(/\d(?=\d{4})/g, '*');
  return record;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you audit data residency choices per tenant and enforce them at scale?
- How would you test DR failover and ensure RTO targets under sustained load?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to architect true cross-project isolation with scalable tenant onboarding, plus governance controls across storage, analytics, and metadata systems.

## Key Concepts
- IAM conditions and per-tenant service accounts
- Tenant-specific data planes (GCS prefixes, BigQuery datasets)
- Private Service Connect and VPC Service Controls for restricted egress
- Data Catalog/Dataplex as a data governance layer
- Dataflow/Test hooks for ingestion, auditing, rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-config: per-tenant IAM condition binding (conceptual)
{
  "binding": {
    "members": ["serviceAccount:tenant-123@project.iam.gserviceaccount.com"],
    "role": "roles/bigquery.dataViewer",
    "condition": {
      "title": "Tenant-specific dataset access",
      "expression": "resource.name.startsWith('projects/_/datasets/tenant_123_')"
    }
  }
}
```
